Restoring dimensions, $\boxed{\frac{d}{dt}\expect{L}
=\frac{i}{\hbar}\expect{[H,L]}
=-\frac{i}{\hbar}\expect{[L,H]}}.$ If $L$ itself depends explicitly on time, the general equation includes the additional term $\expect{\partial L/\partial t}$. Here $L$ is fixed.

